    <title>Perl update strategy</title>
    <meta name="maintainer" content="daria.vladykina@suse.com" its:translate="no"/>
    <abstract>
      <para>
       Perl is a high-level, general-purpose programming language, originally developed for text 
       manipulation, that is now used for system administration, Web development and network programming.
      </para>
    </abstract>
  </info>
  <variablelist>
    <varlistentry>
      <term>Lifecycle category</term>
      <listitem><para>Stable</para></listitem>
    </varlistentry>
    <varlistentry>
      <term>Versions</term>
      <listitem>
        <para>The version shipped with the initial release remains fixed throughout the &suselinux;&nbsp;16 
          lifecycle. Maintenance updates deliver bug and security fixes only, with no major version upgrades 
          planned.</para>
      </listitem>
    </varlistentry>
  </variablelist>
